{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And Noah awoke.</b> The verse does not reveal what was done. And the one who did it was Canaan, and so it was, for Ham saw and did not cover him as his brothers did; he only disclosed the matter, and Canaan heard — but we do not know what he did," "And the meaning of \"his youngest son\" is, according to all evidence, as it says: \"And the sons of Ham: Cush and Mizraim and Put and Canaan\" (Genesis 10:6). Also the vav of \"his son\" refers back to Ham, who is mentioned. Therefore he cursed Canaan. And one who says that Noah cursed his grandson because Elohim had blessed his sons — this is the way of derash:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:01.153322096Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}